<title>UK: Tesco says no plans to cut Irish jobs.</title>
<headline>Tesco says no plans to cut Irish jobs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tesco Plc said on Friday that its 630 million stg purchase of Irish retailing businesses from Associated British Foods Plc would likely enhance earnings from 1998.</p>
<p>Tesco executives told a news conference that it estimated the costs of the deal at 40 million stg and said the company had no current plans to cut jobs.  </p>
<p>&quot;There will be no earnings dilution in 1997, and there will be potential for enhancement thereafter,&quot; Tesco chairman Ian MacLaurin told reporters.</p>
<p>Finance director David Reid estimated the costs of the deal at some 40 million stg, and said, &quot;There are no plans to reduce staff numbers currently.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
